    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d177">

                <pb facs="0336" n="264" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg264"/>

                <head>No. 52.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. West
                        to Earl Granville.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-04-11"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 11, 1882</date>.
                        (Received April 24.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: With reference to my dispatch of the
                    28th ultimo, I have the honor to inclose herewith to your lordship copy of a
                    further note which I have received from the Secretary of State respecting the
                    imprisonment of William Lane.</p>
                <pb facs="0337" n="265" xml:id="pg265"/>
                <p>From the correspondence inclosed in your lordship’s dispatch of the 29th ultimo,
                    it would seem that Mr. Frelinghuysen, in his communications with Mr. Lowell,
                    sought to connect this case with the question of the release of the
                    Irish-American suspects, as I anticipated he might do, as reported to your
                    lordship in my above-mentioned dispatch.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>L. S. SACKVILLE WEST.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d177-a1.xml" xpointer="d177-a1"/>
            </div>
